The main medicinal purpose of washing hands is to purify hands from pathogens (bacteria, viruses or other microorganisms that can cause disease-causing diseases) and chemicals that can cause harm or diseases.
It is very important for people who are dealing or work in the medical field, but it is also an important practice for the general public.
