The World Health Organization (WHO) recommends that new patients should be maintained in stand-alone waiting areas, depending on whether they are a suspected COVID-19 patient. The OSHA (OSHA) recommends those who serve less than a distance of less than six feet and other PPE (PPE), which is likely to develop.
In the United States in the context of a comprehensive, written respiration program consisting of eligibility-test, training, and medical examination should be used with NOIH-appreciative N95 Filating FacePayes Respiratory Accessories or better.
The World Health Organization (WHWHO) does not prescribe the full-fledged exercises as it does not spread through body fluids rather than COVID-19.
The World Health Organization (WHA) recommends the supply of a face mask only to those who enter the country or at an entry point.
The World Health Organization (WHFSA) recommends collecting, caring, caring or transporting respiratory samples from COVID-19 patients without aerosal-making practices.
N-95 or FFP2 (FFP2) respirator is used instead of a mask used during surgical conditions.
Since the global supply of personal protective equipment is not insufficient, physical barriers such as telemedicin, clear windows, allowing only those who are engaged in direct care to enter the room with a COVID-19 patient, only personal protective equipment required for specific work, while caring many patients with the same diagnostic, continuing to use the same respirator without removing the same ventilator, monitoring the personal protective equipment supply chain and discriminating asympthetic individuals from using face masks.
Author: Katherine Maher, Chief Administrative Officer, Wikimedia Company
Recipient: All Wikimedia Foundation Employees
[COVID-19] Easing the workload and preparing for the future
Sending Date / Time: 14-March, 2020, 00:24 UTC
LIC0: No rights are protected
During this month, we are in a unique environment.
The COVID-19 pandemic makes it clear that the human race is connected to each other on a global scale and the liabilities that we have to deal with.
"We don't have an exemplary precedent, but we are aware that the best reaction is to work with global empathy, cooperation and social structure in the company's core."
The friendship and concern we've seen among all of our co-workers through email, calls, and chatting is a significant testament to the fact that we're fortunate to work with amazing people.
There's nothing to be proud and grateful to all of you.
Last week, someone complimented me on my work.
They reminded me how important it is for the world to now look to Wikipedia for the sake of information, and it is an energivable identification to keep these important resources available to everyone online.
It's your job that makes this possible, whether it's a continuing maintenance of platforms or paying our peers or helping our communities to stay safe.
Wikipedia's information is more important to the world.
It's not just how we're going to react, it's how we're making a meaningful impact in the world.
Keeping in mind the importance of this task and your role in it, we will make some significant changes in the way we work together this week.
Changes in our work and action plans
As Robin mentioned earlier, the C-trees met last night to discuss our approach and the plans for the coming days and the months.
We discussed in that conversation about what we consider to be the appropriate answer to the situation we are confronted and the best way to stabilise the company at this time.
We wanted to get rid of stress and support our work for a long period of time.
If you want to reduce your severity, it's okay.
All employees, contractors and contract workers:
4 hours a pear or 20 hours a per cerek.
"We haven't announced a holiday – if you generally want to work more than the time you are working, the task will take full advantage to you."
However, the world is currently unpredictabled that you may want to be supportive of loved ones, you may want to go shopping for groceries or go to the doctor, but your well-being is our priority.
We don't keep track of your time.
Don't go to work if you're sick.
We need to keep that, but we're talking about it.
There is no need a medical holiday or PTO – help your team to edit calendars and action plans to ensure attention is focused on key areas of the task and send a message to your manager.
(If you're tested positive for COVID-19, please let me know Bryan in T&C Ops (T&C Ops), which will help you provide the support you need and ensure that you get the right attention to your level of management).
A full amount will be paid to those who work for hours.
As we said earlier, we reaffirm our contractors to carry out the promise we made to large-stage employees according to the work time.
Salaries will be provided to everyone on the basis of normal working hours.
This includes the fact that you are sick and unable to work.
If you want to work, we will support you.
There are a lot of people who are trying to get rid of the stress that surrounds us.
The work that we are doing, especially in such cases, can yield unforeseen results.
It's about self-defection.
Our request that you need to get in touch with your manager will come to know what to expect and then fix accordingly.
Some tasks are considered to be necessary.
There are a few things we need to keep doing.
SRE, HR Ops Trust & Security, and Fundraising Committees (including others) perform important tasks that are necessary for additional support.
Let us start a process with all the departments to evaluate the present objectives and change our focus on supporting what is essential for our mission.
There is a lot of work to be done for all of us and we will all now pay attention to the most important projects.
Deletion will be reduced later.
"We didn't plan to work ""twubly time to catch the loss"" after the end of the pandemic."
There is no waiting for additional hours to reach an indefinite deadline.
"We accept that the environment has changed and will work to set new goals and chronologies in suitable locations.
What is AP – Annual Planning?
In order to adapt to the new system and the daily working hours, we intend to change the deadline for the implementation of our 2020-2021 annual plans.
Our mission is to propose an extension of the 2019-2020 scheme, which gives more time for the next few weeks to plan to prioritize important work for employees, self-defense and care of loved ones.
This deadline extension greatly reduces the current planning workload and pressure in the entire company.
We will introduce our project to the executive committee next week, and as soon as the confirmation is received, we will update on the next phases with the representatives and groups.
Thanks to the APP team for taking the lead.
Observation of Office Status, Influence and Cleaning
Last week we came to know that one of our co-workers from San Francisco was subjected to the COVID-19 virus.
However, as a precautionary measure, we cleaned with an anti-mibrial cleaning team to disinfection on all surfaces at the San Francisco office.
They used a hospital-grade pathogen-proof mixture to disinfection in the surfaces, the home room and the lifts that approach our site.
The moral or legitimatial obligation ethical protocol is maintained in this building to ensure the safety of the residents.
When we decide to return to work, we are comforted to know that the office will be ready.
Our TC (DC) office is located in a Wework. They share their COVID-19-based ethics with us as well as all D.C (DC) personnel.
As of last week, our D.C (DC) office switched to a full-fled distance level system in line with a shared guidance with San Francisco.
We are also debugging about leasing a place in Brooklyn, as some colleagues from our New New York City are familiar.
These discussions will continue, but may be delayed.
For the first time, some of our colleagues are working from a distance.
Our long-distance peers will be aware that this is an adjustment and wanted to give you some advice:
The length of the meetings should be limited to a maximum increase of one or two hours.
If require long-term sessions, examine how they can be divided into multi-daying sessions.
To clearly define the necessity of the meeting, to create an action plan, and pass things that need to be studied in advance.
Make the video default with tools such as Google Docs and Zoom to simplify live connection and connectivity.
Someone to formally arrange previous appointments, someone to monitor the questions that arise during the chat and tracing the speaker's list and to help him to take notes (or jointly taking notes).
If you don't need a comfortable headset, send an email for technical assistance.
You will be able to get the money you've been paid.
Join the ��#Remotities Channel in Slock to talk to your peers about distributed jobs
The Human Resource Operations Committee (HRC) is taking steps to conduct webinar-based ergonomic guidance to support the increased level of shared work throughout the company.
Last week, we called on all social grant recipients to call for annunciation until the World Health Organization (WHA) announces that public events, such as Editathons, with the financial assistance of Wikimedia.
We made it clear to them that based on our request for cancellation and other restrictions, we did not understand that it is not possible to complete the subsidy measures accepted by them and no one will be penalised for the delay or change in achieving those targets.
Let's pursue additional guidelines on Wikimania and other regional and thematic social conferences this week.
When it comes to the global community, it has become clear that this disorder has generally created misery rather than helping their own communities, wikimedia and others focus on their own communities.
CRD (CRT) is in the process of setting up a page on Meta-Wike to help the community, keep an account with the future, monitor the impact and follow our communications.
Continuing information on COVID-19 related issues
On the next Thursday, at 14:0:00 UTC / 07: 00 PT, we will send an invitation to your calendars to take part in a special staff meeting.
You can use this time to share additional updates, answer your questions, and spend a little time with each other.
We are ready to do our best in this regard.
Meanwhile, you can get some information from this email and you can find information related to all essential COVID-19 related information on the Office wiki.
CRT (CRT) will update these pages from time to time and process all the information to be available in one place.
We also maintain common communication with employees living in countries currently having a significant impact.
If you have questions about travel, events, a major task segment or an insurance-based challenge or necessary assistance, please don't hesitate to notify the CRD or work together.
We are here to provide the necessary support and cooperation.
If you have confidential or subtle information, please send an email to HR-International Global Operations Director Bryan Juden.
These changes should not be seen as an act of abandoning our duties and duties.
On the other hand, it is a recognition that at this junct time, our work and diducations will have to be reversed in an unprecedented manner.
We are of the view that these steps are necessary to support each other to continue to work, to provide the necessary support to our movement and to provide them with the service they are facing.
We will be waiting for the work to be completed.
For the time being, it's time to be supportive of each other and for important jobs that will come in a few weeks or as possible in a few months.
We all we need to do to achieve it, so we want you to take the opportunity to do as well as you and your family at the time of need and take proper care of yourself and your family.
"Please, don't wash your hands and don't tweak your face."
